0.28601","daa1876316641.u64.30958"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The intra-group carve-out attaches to the Type 9 regulated-activity definition and requires services solely to the specified related entities. The selected control receives the classification after carve-outs are resolved. Ordinary-course business guidance is qualified and does not establish a separate unconditional exemption.","source_unit_ids":["daa1876316641.u39.28171","daa1876316641.u40.28601"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"All three Q3 factors must be present. 'Should not in the ordinary course', 'may be regarded', 'increases the likelihood', 'typically', and 'primarily' retain their qualified force. The result tests the stated trigger, not possession of a licence or actual unlawful conduct.","source_unit_ids":["daa1876316641.u38.27681","daa1876316641.u40.28601","daa1876316641.u53.30093","daa1876316641.u65.31118"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"2020-01-07 identifies the referenced Circular; 2020-09-08 is the FAQ update date. Neither supplies an effective-date threshold or a period over which continuity must be assessed.","source_unit_ids":["daa1876316641.u1.25828","daa1876316641.u40.28601","daa1876316641.u80.31413"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"The Ordinance and Circular are referenced but absent. Dependency missing.b8f9c69dd226e4db3f4557d7 has no supplied content or source hash, so its identity and effect cannot be determined. Regulated-activity classification and business assessment remain judgment-dependent inputs, not findings established by this packet.","source_unit_ids":["daa1876316641.u1.25828","daa1876316641.u38.27681","daa1876316641.u39.28171","daa1876316641.u40.28601","daa1876316641.u64.30958"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the negation in Q3's ordinary-course guidance extend to 'have the pursuit of profit as its business objective', and how should a re